How do you think there's a proper way to update the node's form values ​​when clicking 'Save' in the sidebar footer?

The idea is that the node doesn't change its value with each change, but rather that the button click updates all the changes made by the node.

In this case, `handleSave` would handle the logic for updating the node's values.

```
  const footer = (
        <Flex>
            <Button
            onClick={handleSave}
            >
                Save</Button>
        </Flex>
    );

    return (
        <SideSheet
            title={nodeRender?.node.getNodeRegistry().name}
            mask={false} visible={!!nodeRender} onCancel={handleClose}
            footer={footer}
            closeOnEsc
        >
            <IsSidebarContext.Provider value={true}>{content}</IsSidebarContext.Provider>
        </SideSheet>
    );
```

